From 04231bd21894db71bcc36e1737fd1215f5241942 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:33:35 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] kcm_kwinscreenedges: preview first, three noun
 sections, scans after the first frame

Page type: Form with a preview (QtWidgets kept, docs/page-design.md 8: QFormLayout, bold section titles, no group frames).
kcfg keys (kwinrc Windows/ElectricBorder*, ScreenEdges/*, EdgeBarrier/*, effect and script BorderActivate lists), the edge
actions, D-Bus reconfigure calls and plugin id are unchanged. Made consistent with kcm_kwintouchscreen (same source dir): same
order (info line, preview, hint under the preview), same widget names and spacing.

Moved / renamed (main.ui):
- Order by use: info line, preview, then "Window Dragging" (Maximize, Tile, quarter tiling ratio indented under Tile),
  "Edge Behavior" (switch desktop, activation delay, reactivation delay, remain active when fullscreen), "Multiple Screens"
  (corner barrier, edge barrier). Was: one run of rows under the preview with labels "Maximize:", "Tile:", "Behavior:".
- Rows with a label column holding a one-word noun and a checkbox with the sentence are now plain checkboxes:
  "Maximize windows dragged to the top edge", "Tile windows dragged to the left or right edge"; "Corner barrier" got its own
  checkbox text (was an empty checkbox beside a "Corner barrier:" label).
- New hint under the preview: "Click an edge or corner of the preview to choose its action." (the preview is the main
  control and nothing said it is clickable). Info line: "Push the mouse pointer against a screen edge or corner to run an action."
- Old wording added to the aliases in ia/layout.json; relabel table inventory/relabel/kcm_kwinscreenedges.tsv. Markers on
  the changed checkboxes and on the weak rows (edge-action, per-edge keys). Inventory --strict: 33 ok, 0 lost.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-013 (grouped, indented dependent option), HIG-019, HIG-057. Page-design 2, 3, 8.

Speed cause (code): the KWinScreenEdgesConfig constructor ran monitorInit() (main.cpp), which iterates kwin/builtin-effects
reading every effect JSON, lists scripted effect and script packages with KPackage and creates one KConfigSkeleton per
effect/script, all before the first frame. Now it runs in a QTimer::singleShot(0) after the constructor and then loads the
edge actions; save() is ignored until then (it would write "None" for every edge from empty menus).
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet. Unconfirmed without a build: QFormLayout colspan rows and
the Qt::AlignHCenter hint label in uic output; the ui connections to label_1 and the ratio label (kept by name).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
